WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:05.973
"Do the Side Effects of Ozempic (Semaglutide)
Outweigh the Benefits?"

00:00:07.174 --> 00:00:08.842
"Thinner is better,"

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.344
is the conventional wisdom
when it comes

00:00:10.344 --> 00:00:12.613
to minimizing the risk
of cardiovascular events

00:00:12.613 --> 00:00:14.414
like heart attacks and strokes,

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:15.549
but there have been cases

00:00:15.549 --> 00:00:16.717
where weight loss medications

00:00:16.717 --> 00:00:19.753
actually led to increased
cardiovascular risk

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:22.222
despite significant
reductions in body fat.

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:23.590
So, we can’t just assume

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.926
drug-induced weight loss
will help.

00:00:25.926 --> 00:00:28.929
Now, if it’s true
that GLP-1 drugs, like Ozempic,

00:00:28.929 --> 00:00:31.098
reduce cardiovascular events,

00:00:31.098 --> 00:00:33.367
which are some
of our leading causes of death,

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:36.203
then that benefit
would significantly overwhelm

00:00:36.203 --> 00:00:38.605
the risk of almost any amount
of thyroid cancer

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:40.073
these drugs may cause.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:42.209
Let’s look at the data.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.878
Some major trials have found

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:47.848
that among high-risk
individuals with diabetes,

00:00:47.848 --> 00:00:50.717
risk of cardiovascular events
were significantly lower

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.786
among those
randomized to Ozempic

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:54.922
compared to placebo injections,

00:00:54.922 --> 00:00:56.890
but other trials did not.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.293
Interesting how
the lack of benefit was spun

00:00:59.293 --> 00:01:02.796
by saying, "Hey,
it’s not inferior to placebo."

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.431
But that was the main concern,

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:06.433
that Ozempic, like some
other weight loss drugs,

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:08.936
could actually increase
cardiovascular disease.

00:01:08.936 --> 00:01:12.906
So, it was considered a relief
that it had no effect.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.375
Enough evidence
of benefit accrued, though,

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:17.377
that Ozempic
and another GLP-1 drug

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:20.147
were approved
for cardiovascular protection

00:01:20.147 --> 00:01:24.151
among individuals
with Type II diabetes.

00:01:24.151 --> 00:01:26.119
Remember, these were
originally prescribed

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:27.321
as diabetes drugs.

00:01:27.321 --> 00:01:30.757
So, maybe users reduced
their cardiovascular risk

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.592
just by lowering
their blood sugars

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:35.228
rather than
by lowering their weight.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:38.231
What we want to know is this.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:39.766
What is the effect of Ozempic

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.969
on cardiovascular outcomes
in obesity

00:01:41.969 --> 00:01:44.538
for people without diabetes?

00:01:44.538 --> 00:01:46.440
And, in patients

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.842
who have preexisting
cardiovascular disease,

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.410
and are overweight or obese,

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.412
but do not have diabetes,

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.982
those randomized
to weight loss doses of Ozempic

00:01:54.982 --> 00:01:56.817
had an overall lower rate

00:01:56.817 --> 00:01:58.986
of either having
a cardiovascular event,

00:01:58.986 --> 00:02:00.087
like a heart attack or stroke,

00:02:00.087 --> 00:02:03.223
or dying from it,
compared to placebo.

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:04.391
That’s exciting,

00:02:04.391 --> 00:02:06.793
but we have to highlight
another caveat, though.

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.028
The researchers
just looked at

00:02:08.028 --> 00:02:11.932
those with preexisting
cardiovascular disease.

00:02:11.932 --> 00:02:14.134
That is an important
limitation of these findings.

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:15.402
The effects of these
weight-loss drugs

00:02:15.402 --> 00:02:17.537
on the prevention
of cardiovascular events

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:20.407
in those without diagnosed
atherosclerotic disease

00:02:20.407 --> 00:02:23.310
have not yet been determined.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.178
Still, a lot
of overweight people

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.313
have a history of heart attack,

00:02:26.313 --> 00:02:28.115
stroke,
or peripheral vascular disease.

00:02:28.115 --> 00:02:29.716
So, how big is the benefit?

00:02:30.651 --> 00:02:32.519
Over a period of a few years,

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:34.755
8% of people
with cardiovascular disease

00:02:34.755 --> 00:02:36.890
suffered another event
on the placebo,

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.926
but only 6.5%
suffered a subsequent event

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.361
on the drug.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:45.198
Going from 8 to 6.5
is a 20% drop.

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:48.335
You can see it clearly
if you zoom in.

00:02:48.335 --> 00:02:50.637
Unfortunately,
many news stories focused on

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:52.906
that 20% relative risk reduction

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:55.008
rather than on
the absolute risk reduction

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.977
of 1.5%.

00:02:56.977 --> 00:03:00.447
Yes, 8 to 6.5 is a 20% drop,

00:03:00.447 --> 00:03:01.381
but, at the same time,

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:05.352
you’re really only reducing
your absolute risk by 1.5%.

00:03:05.352 --> 00:03:06.119
In other words,

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:08.288
you’d have to treat
67 people with the drug

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:10.590
for a few years
to prevent one heart attack

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.993
or stroke
or cardiovascular death.

00:03:12.993 --> 00:03:16.363
That may not sound like much
on an individual scale.

00:03:16.363 --> 00:03:17.564
I mean, what are the odds

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:20.000
you’re going to be
that 1 in 67th person?

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.903
But on a population scale,
it’s huge.

00:03:22.903 --> 00:03:24.104
In fact, it’s right up there

00:03:24.104 --> 00:03:26.173
with cholesterol-lowering
statin drugs,

00:03:26.173 --> 00:03:27.741
which have
an absolute risk reduction

00:03:27.741 --> 00:03:30.644
in the same 1.5% ballpark.

00:03:30.644 --> 00:03:32.746
So, indeed, in March 2024,

00:03:32.746 --> 00:03:33.814
the Food and Drug Administration

00:03:33.814 --> 00:03:35.315
approved high-dose Ozempic

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:37.017
for use beyond just weight loss

00:03:37.017 --> 00:03:39.586
but also for reducing
cardiovascular risk

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:44.024
in those with
prior cardiovascular disease.

00:03:44.024 --> 00:03:47.594
So, how do the benefits
and harms stack up?

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:48.795
In the summer of 2024,

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:51.898
the first quantitative
benefit-harm balance analysis

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.200
was published.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.267
The researchers concluded

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:57.003
that for those achieving
a 10% weight loss,

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:59.039
there’s more than a 90% chance

00:03:59.039 --> 00:04:00.640
the benefits outweigh the harms,

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:03.443
though the opposite was found
for only a 5% weight loss.

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:05.245
Here’s how they broke it down.

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:07.948
If 1,000 people
go on these GLP-1 drugs,

00:04:07.948 --> 00:04:10.650
375 would be expected to lose

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.085
at least 10%
of their body weight

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:14.688
with all the ancillary benefits
that would bring.

00:04:14.688 --> 00:04:16.356
On the other side
of the equation,

00:04:16.356 --> 00:04:19.392
41 people would suffer
from abdominal pain,

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:22.162
57 from hair loss,
8 from gallstones,

00:04:22.162 --> 00:04:25.031
118 from constipation,
100 from diarrhea,

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:27.968
22 from dizziness,
84 from an upset stomach,

00:04:27.968 --> 00:04:30.971
46 from excessive burping,
39 from fatigue,

00:04:30.971 --> 00:04:34.107
51 from excessive farting,
13 from headaches,

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.542
17 from low blood sugars,

00:04:35.542 --> 00:04:37.844
4 from reactions
at the injection site.

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:41.114
221 would suffer from nausea,
4 from pancreatitis,

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:44.885
43 from upper abdominal pain,
and 110 from vomiting.

00:04:44.885 --> 00:04:48.155
Now, of course, the net benefit
versus harm calculation

00:04:48.155 --> 00:04:50.123
would be highly dependent on

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:52.926
different people’s willingness
to accept different harms.

00:04:52.926 --> 00:04:55.462
Like a bald guy
isn’t going to be concerned

00:04:55.462 --> 00:04:57.230
about hair loss, for example.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.232
And this also
doesn’t take into account

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:01.768
the fact that
the benefits peter out.

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:03.436
Weight loss stalls after a year,

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:05.238
but the harms may continue.

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:06.973
So, once
you’ve already plateaued

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:08.675
and stop losing weight,

00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:10.143
do you keep taking it

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.978
even though you get
no further weight-loss benefit

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:15.916
but the potential for harm
continues to accumulate?

00:05:15.916 --> 00:05:19.286
We really don’t know about
the long-term harms or benefits

00:05:19.286 --> 00:05:22.556
because some of these drugs
and dosing schedules are so new,

00:05:22.556 --> 00:05:25.559
especially now that the American
Academy of Pediatrics

00:05:25.559 --> 00:05:26.960
has suggested
offering these drugs

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:30.263
for teens and tweens
as young as age 12.

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:32.465
These drugs work
by acting on the brain,

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:34.968
so, who knows what effect
this could have

00:05:34.968 --> 00:05:36.836
on childhood development
and beyond,

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:40.173
if they end up taking them
for the rest of their lives.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:43.276
In the end,
this story is familiar.

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:45.278
A new class
of antidiabetic agents

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:47.280
is rushed to market
and widely promoted

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.648
in the absence
of any evidence

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:50.750
of long-term
beneficial outcomes.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.419
Evidence of harms accumulate,

00:05:52.419 --> 00:05:55.121
but it’s vigorously denied
or discounted.

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:58.558
The manufacturers are expected,
quite unrealistically,

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:01.261
to monitor the safety
of their own products.

00:06:01.261 --> 00:06:02.996
We should be thankful
that those responsible

00:06:02.996 --> 00:06:04.197
for aircraft safety

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:06.766
do not operate
under the same assumption.

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:08.501
Although we now
do have evidence

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.770
of at least near-term benefit
over a few years,

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.073
we cannot assume
long-term safety

00:06:13.073 --> 00:06:15.041
until it has been demonstrated.

